arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115: Add IPA

Tested on a Moto G Power (2021): the firmware loads and authenticates, the
driver sees the modem start, and rmnet_ipa0 appears. No data has passed
through it, as that takes a SIM, which is the reason to read this as "the
driver comes up" and no more than that.

On this SoC, restarting the modem with the IPA runtime suspended freezes
the whole system, which "net: ipa: Keep the IPA powered while the modem
boots, every time" fixes. That's sent separately to netdev, and is needed
before this is safe to use with modem restarts.
